WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.319
The second question NOSHASHI answers is: could you actually get out of a position?

2
00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:09.319
The answer is in the order book, but not in the number most tools show.

3
00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:15.007
The XRP Ledger has had a built-in exchange since twenty twelve.

4
00:00:15.007 --> 00:00:22.223
Anyone can post an offer, and all the offers for one pair form an order book: bids on one side, asks on the other.

5
00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:28.427
The average of the best bid and best ask is the mid price, and the gap between them is the spread.

6
00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:32.233
Here is the catch most tools miss.

7
00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:37.376
An offer stays on the book even after its owner no longer has the funds to fill it.

8
00:00:37.376 --> 00:00:39.855
It is still listed, but it cannot trade.

9
00:00:40.305 --> 00:00:42.782
Say three offers each list ten thousand.

10
00:00:42.782 --> 00:00:48.667
The first owner holds ten thousand, the second holds five hundred, and the third holds nothing.

11
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:51.198
Listed depth says thirty thousand.

12
00:00:51.198 --> 00:00:55.911
Funded depth, what owners can actually deliver, is ten thousand five hundred.

13
00:00:55.911 --> 00:01:00.317
Try to sell twenty thousand into that book and most of it will not fill.

14
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:03.546
NOSHASHI is not guessing.

15
00:01:03.546 --> 00:01:12.166
When a server returns a book, any offer whose owner cannot cover it carries an extra field, taker gets funded, showing what they really have.

16
00:01:12.166 --> 00:01:16.140
NOSHASHI adds up those funded amounts instead of the listed ones.

17
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:28.394
Here are six real pairs, measured on the eighth of September twenty twenty-six at ledger one hundred six million, eight hundred fifty thousand, two hundred sixty-six.

18
00:01:28.394 --> 00:01:33.925
The ratio is listed depth divided by funded depth, within ten percent of the mid price.

19
00:01:34.375 --> 00:01:42.141
The deep stablecoin books are close to honest: Bitstamp and GateHub dollars are at one point zero and one point one times.

20
00:01:42.591 --> 00:01:44.704
The long tail is where the gap lives.

21
00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:53.385
The Sologenic book listed about two and a half thousand times more than was funded, and the Bitstamp bitcoin book had nothing funded in the band at all.

22
00:01:53.835 --> 00:01:56.907
The median across the six was four point four times.

23
00:01:58.607 --> 00:02:00.232
Three honest disclosures.

24
00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:05.626
The ten percent band is a parameter we chose, and a wider band gives a smaller gap.

25
00:02:06.076 --> 00:02:11.665
Automated market maker pools are left out, so where a pool exists, the real exit is better.

26
00:02:12.115 --> 00:02:15.358
And a server returns at most sixty price levels of a book.

27
00:02:15.808 --> 00:02:17.593
All three push the gap upward.

28
00:02:17.593 --> 00:02:21.996
Books change every few seconds, so re-measure before you quote any figure.

29
00:02:21.996 --> 00:02:26.517
In the app, the Order Book screen does this with one button: Read this book.
